    "nodes": {
      "1": {
        "attributes": {
          "font-size": {
            "type": "number",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "GATE\n\nThe Gate has a cases that you can open an close by changing the value on the inlet. If one case is open, the others will be closed. Cases can be selected by inputing Bool's, Float's or Int's. The Gate node is meant to be used with signals although it will accept events. When working with events it's better to use the Switch node instead.\n\n- Patch Explained -\n• We have 4 sines runnning at different speeds.\n• In the top part of the patch we're using an Int node to function as a selector for the gate.\n• The selected case opens and the signal flows through, affecting the radius of the circle.\n• In this example the Gate functions as a speed regulator with different speeds at every case.\n• In the bottom part of the patch we see another Gate. This gate is controlled by a Bool.\n• This gate will let through either the sine with a frequency of 1 or the sine with a frequency of 0.25, modulating the Fish Eye effect."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 293.384033203125,
          "width": 833,
          "x": 57.18053436279297,
          "y": -41.83314895629883
        },
